      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the early 1790s, settlers built a sawmill and gristmill at the creek confluence, turning the fast‑flowing waters into a local industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/spring_mills_pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By the early 1800s, a blacksmith shop, log schoolhouse, inn, and sawmill made Spring Mills a bustling milling and trade hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/spring_mills_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early churches like the Methodist Episcopal and Presbyterian, plus the Spring Mills Academy, reflected a community rooted in German and Scotch‑Irish traditions.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/spring_mills_pennsylvania",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Spring Mills sits in the Ridge and Valley province of the Appalachians, where parallel ridges carve the Penns Valley.",
